    "title": "Hayneville Arson Case Now Homicide After Woman Found Shot in Burned Home - NewsBreak",
    "text": "9 hours ago Authorities in Lowndes County, Alabama, have reclassified an arson case as a homicide. Investigators determined that a woman found in a burned home on Rivers Drive in Hayneville had been shot multiple times before the fire. The victim was identified as Denisha Lyles of Tallassee. Officials believe the fire was set after her death, and an accelerant was used.\nThe incident took place on November 16, 2025, though some records list November 15. Fire crews from White Hall and Fort Deposit responded, and the Alabama State Fire Marshal’s Office joined the investigation. A fire K-9 detected evidence of arson, leading authorities to treat the case as suspicious. The investigation is ongoing as officials work to identify and locate a suspect.\nVisit here for more details This post includes content assisted by AI tools. Please refer to the source for verification and additional information. Learn more.",
